WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:01.970
- The first shot of the movie
shows us a delivery truck

00:00:01.970 --> 00:00:03.180
with Illinois license plates

00:00:03.180 --> 00:00:05.240
but this movie doesn't
take place in Illinois.

00:00:05.240 --> 00:00:06.444
This is actually a little sign for fans

00:00:06.444 --> 00:00:08.730
that Curse of Chucky would
take the franchise back

00:00:08.730 --> 00:00:09.563
to its roots,

00:00:09.563 --> 00:00:10.900
that this entry would return to horror

00:00:10.900 --> 00:00:13.790
by focusing on suspense and
psychological manipulation more

00:00:13.790 --> 00:00:15.500
in line with the first
movie, Child's Play,

00:00:15.500 --> 00:00:17.230
which took place in Chicago, Illinois.

00:00:17.230 --> 00:00:19.300
Appropriately, this movie
would honor the original

00:00:19.300 --> 00:00:21.370
in many ways, from new
characters filling the shoes

00:00:21.370 --> 00:00:22.300
of classic characters,

00:00:22.300 --> 00:00:24.710
bringing back iconic kills
and even secrets hidden

00:00:24.710 --> 00:00:26.440
on computer screens and in the background

00:00:26.440 --> 00:00:27.750
of an old friend's apartment.

00:00:27.750 --> 00:00:30.310
To learn about all the ways
this movie brought back elements

00:00:30.310 --> 00:00:31.600
of Child's Play and many

00:00:31.600 --> 00:00:32.830
other details you might have missed,

00:00:32.830 --> 00:00:35.020
stick around to the end of this video.

00:00:35.020 --> 00:00:37.454
This video is sponsored by Amazon Music.

00:00:37.454 --> 00:00:40.037
(upbeat music)

00:00:43.270 --> 00:00:44.800
I've been excited to do this episode

00:00:44.800 --> 00:00:45.680
ever since I started

00:00:45.680 --> 00:00:47.780
covering the Chucky
franchise two years ago,

00:00:47.780 --> 00:00:49.860
because this is by far
the best Chucky movie.

00:00:49.860 --> 00:00:51.760
I know I'm not supposed to say my opinion,

00:00:51.760 --> 00:00:53.380
but come on, it's not even close.

00:00:53.380 --> 00:00:54.674
If you didn't already
know, you may be surprised

00:00:54.674 --> 00:00:56.190
to learn that Curse was directed

00:00:56.190 --> 00:00:57.730
by the same director who did Seed.

00:00:57.730 --> 00:00:59.480
These movies could not be more different,

00:00:59.480 --> 00:01:02.370
Seed was a raunchy, colorful
over-the-top dark comedy

00:01:02.370 --> 00:01:05.300
while Curse is a dark,
subdued, tragic suspense film.

00:01:05.300 --> 00:01:06.530
But you may be less surprised

00:01:06.530 --> 00:01:08.300
by this quick sobering-up that takes place

00:01:08.300 --> 00:01:10.620
between these two if you
know who that director is,

00:01:10.620 --> 00:01:13.210
it's Don Mancini, the
original writer and creator

00:01:13.210 --> 00:01:14.043
of Child's Play.

00:01:14.043 --> 00:01:16.110
As I mentioned, the tone
of this movie goes back

00:01:16.110 --> 00:01:17.840
towards that 1988 original

00:01:17.840 --> 00:01:19.830
but what I didn't mention is it goes past

00:01:19.830 --> 00:01:21.930
that and keeps going
into its own territory

00:01:21.930 --> 00:01:23.120
and in my opinion this is

00:01:23.120 --> 00:01:24.590
how you play to Chucky's strengths.

00:01:24.590 --> 00:01:26.510
Of course, this is not a review.

00:01:26.510 --> 00:01:27.700
You're here for Things You Missed,

00:01:27.700 --> 00:01:29.857
so why don't we get back into them?

00:01:29.857 --> 00:01:32.690
(knives scraping)

00:01:35.010 --> 00:01:36.290
For the first time in the franchise,

00:01:36.290 --> 00:01:38.440
we don't start with Chucky
coming back to life,

00:01:38.440 --> 00:01:40.550
but rather, by meeting
our other characters,

00:01:40.550 --> 00:01:42.890
starting with a paraplegic
woman named Nica Pierce

00:01:42.890 --> 00:01:44.250
and her mom, Sarah Pierce.

00:01:44.250 --> 00:01:45.910
We see that Sarah has some health issues,

00:01:45.910 --> 00:01:47.450
because her bedside table is filled

00:01:47.450 --> 00:01:49.610
with anxiety medications
and antidepressants.

00:01:49.610 --> 00:01:51.560
This is an important detail
that comes back later

00:01:51.560 --> 00:01:52.460
and it helps cast doubt

00:01:52.460 --> 00:01:54.410
on the idea that Chucky is really alive.

00:01:54.410 --> 00:01:55.610
In the original Child's Play,

00:01:55.610 --> 00:01:57.410
we as the audience know
that Chucky is alive

00:01:57.410 --> 00:01:59.720
but the adults in the story
don't believe that he is.

00:01:59.720 --> 00:02:01.220
Curse puts its own twist on this

00:02:01.220 --> 00:02:03.330
by making the audience
doubt that Chucky is alive.

00:02:03.330 --> 00:02:05.160
Obviously if you've seen
a Chucky movie before,

00:02:05.160 --> 00:02:07.170
you go into this one
thinking that he is alive,

00:02:07.170 --> 00:02:08.080
just like all the others,

00:02:08.080 --> 00:02:10.260
but when we don't see proof
of that until much later,

00:02:10.260 --> 00:02:11.450
you start to wonder if one

00:02:11.450 --> 00:02:13.900
of the human characters is
simply using a Good Guy doll

00:02:13.900 --> 00:02:16.200
to cover up his or her
own criminal actions.

00:02:16.200 --> 00:02:18.110
I just wish they would have
left out this opening credit

00:02:18.110 --> 00:02:20.170
that says Brad Dourif
as the voice of Chucky.

00:02:20.170 --> 00:02:22.340
I get why they have to put
that in there contractually,

00:02:22.340 --> 00:02:23.939
but it would have been better
if the movie made us doubt

00:02:23.939 --> 00:02:26.430
that this doll was the
real Chucky and then hit us

00:02:26.430 --> 00:02:28.630
with that, surprise,
actually it is Chucky.

00:02:28.630 --> 00:02:30.260
You could get rid of a
couple other shots too

00:02:30.260 --> 00:02:31.679
to really go all in on the mystery aspect

00:02:31.679 --> 00:02:33.962
but one thing you may have
noticed was the elevator

00:02:33.962 --> 00:02:35.263
inside of Nica's house.

00:02:35.263 --> 00:02:37.610
It's the same kind of
old-fashioned elevator seen

00:02:37.610 --> 00:02:39.560
in The Barclay's apartment
in the first movie.

00:02:39.560 --> 00:02:41.160
We also see a Chucky POV

00:02:41.160 --> 00:02:43.150
which I don't think we've
seen since Child's Play 1,

00:02:43.150 --> 00:02:44.790
we see Charles Lee Ray's human form

00:02:44.790 --> 00:02:46.960
that we haven't seen since
the first one and near the end

00:02:46.960 --> 00:02:47.793
of the movie,

00:02:47.793 --> 00:02:48.690
Nica stabs the Chucky doll

00:02:48.690 --> 00:02:51.010
with a knife and the fluff
from inside the doll shoots up

00:02:51.010 --> 00:02:53.210
in the air and then
slowly floats down on her.

00:02:53.210 --> 00:02:54.082
It almost looks like snow.

00:02:54.082 --> 00:02:56.940
The first movie takes
place entirely in the snow.

00:02:56.940 --> 00:02:58.270
But Curse isn't just here

00:02:58.270 --> 00:03:00.950
for superficial visual callbacks to 1988.

00:03:00.950 --> 00:03:02.500
If you think about the character dynamics,

00:03:02.500 --> 00:03:03.920
there are even more similarities.

00:03:03.920 --> 00:03:06.640
For one, Chucky finally has
a new best friend to the end,

00:03:06.640 --> 00:03:09.290
that is, a young kid that he
psychologically manipulates.

00:03:09.290 --> 00:03:10.430
Instead of Andy this time,

00:03:10.430 --> 00:03:11.830
it's the little girl, Alice.

00:03:11.830 --> 00:03:12.859
He keeps his true nature a secret

00:03:12.859 --> 00:03:15.430
by only communicating
with her and through her

00:03:15.430 --> 00:03:16.900
because she's too young to understand

00:03:16.900 --> 00:03:18.550
that dolls shouldn't be sentient.

00:03:19.964 --> 00:03:22.540
- Oh, Chucky wants to
know what's for dinner.

00:03:22.540 --> 00:03:26.243
- Chucky wants to watch
the nine o'clock news.

00:03:27.110 --> 00:03:29.440
- And he doesn't hold
back any graphic language.

00:03:29.440 --> 00:03:31.250
- He said that life's a (upbeat tone)

00:03:31.250 --> 00:03:34.480
and then you die,
bleeding like a stuck pig.

00:03:34.480 --> 00:03:36.660
- He said Aunt Maggie
was a real (upbeat one)

00:03:36.660 --> 00:03:39.120
and got what she deserved.

00:03:39.120 --> 00:03:41.280
- In addition to the child
to doll relationship,

00:03:41.280 --> 00:03:43.140
the child in each movie has another adult

00:03:43.140 --> 00:03:43.973
who's close to them.

00:03:43.973 --> 00:03:44.806
In Curse of Chucky,

00:03:44.806 --> 00:03:46.640
Alice has a special
bond with her Aunt Nica

00:03:46.640 --> 00:03:47.690
and in Child's Play,

00:03:47.690 --> 00:03:49.950
Andy has his Aunt Maggie,
who isn't really his Aunt

00:03:49.950 --> 00:03:51.530
but she's such a close family friend

00:03:51.530 --> 00:03:52.840
that he calls her as such.

00:03:52.840 --> 00:03:54.400
In reality, she's more of a nanny

00:03:54.400 --> 00:03:56.190
and Curse also has a dedicated nanny,

00:03:56.190 --> 00:03:58.460
so that role is kind of
split into two characters

00:03:58.460 --> 00:03:59.781
but another similarity is what happens

00:03:59.781 --> 00:04:01.750
to each respective aunt character.

00:04:01.750 --> 00:04:03.580
In Child's Play, Chucky pushes Aunt Maggie

00:04:03.580 --> 00:04:05.280
through the window of
the high rise apartment

00:04:05.280 --> 00:04:07.150
and in Curse, he rolls
Aunt Nica's wheelchair

00:04:07.150 --> 00:04:07.983
through a railing,

00:04:07.983 --> 00:04:10.100
sending her off the second
floor landing in the foyer.

00:04:10.100 --> 00:04:11.440
If you're an observant Chucky fan,

00:04:11.440 --> 00:04:13.590
you may have noticed the
first big confirmation

00:04:13.590 --> 00:04:15.250
that Chucky is actually alive.

00:04:15.250 --> 00:04:16.580
When Alice finds him in the bathroom,

00:04:16.580 --> 00:04:17.950
he's got bloodshot eyes.

00:04:17.950 --> 00:04:19.350
It's actually in the previous movie,

00:04:19.350 --> 00:04:21.820
Seed of Chucky, that we see
what happens to the dolls' eyes

00:04:21.820 --> 00:04:23.730
when the awakening ritual
is performed on them.

00:04:23.730 --> 00:04:25.276
So this means that Alice's new doll is

00:04:25.276 --> 00:04:26.912
in fact possessed like the dolls

00:04:26.912 --> 00:04:28.660
we've seen throughout the franchise.

00:04:28.660 --> 00:04:30.560
When Chucky starts taking
victims at the house,

00:04:30.560 --> 00:04:31.830
Nica's brother in law, Ian,

00:04:31.830 --> 00:04:33.450
starts to point the finger at her.

00:04:33.450 --> 00:04:34.920
The situation is somewhat similar

00:04:34.920 --> 00:04:37.130
to the plot of the 1982 film, The Thing,

00:04:37.130 --> 00:04:38.400
featuring Richard Masur.

00:04:38.400 --> 00:04:40.315
It makes me wonder if the
name of Nica's physician,

00:04:40.315 --> 00:04:43.270
Dr. Masur is an intentional reference.

00:04:43.270 --> 00:04:45.020
- Dr. Masur said I was fine.

00:04:45.020 --> 00:04:46.930
- Dr. Masur said that extreme stress,

00:04:46.930 --> 00:04:49.140
any kind of even mild shock-

00:04:49.140 --> 00:04:50.880
- They pronounce it a little
bit funny in the movie,

00:04:50.880 --> 00:04:52.650
but if you look at the
script and subtitles,

00:04:52.650 --> 00:04:53.590
it is spelled the same way

00:04:53.590 --> 00:04:55.160
that Richard Masur spells his name.

00:04:55.160 --> 00:04:56.920
It might not be an intentional reference,

00:04:56.920 --> 00:04:58.270
but it's an uncommon enough name

00:04:58.270 --> 00:04:59.940
to make me entertain the possibility.

00:04:59.940 --> 00:05:01.780
After the very tense dinner scene,

00:05:01.780 --> 00:05:03.780
Nica brings the doll
upstairs in the elevator

00:05:03.780 --> 00:05:05.880
when the power goes out, and
when the lights come back on,

00:05:05.880 --> 00:05:08.609
she sees this.

00:05:08.609 --> 00:05:10.590
(doll laughing)

00:05:10.590 --> 00:05:13.010
The doll's head had
spun around 180 degrees,

00:05:13.010 --> 00:05:15.853
leading to this very
unsettling moment with Alice.

00:05:18.420 --> 00:05:20.000
- Hey, wanna play?

00:05:20.000 --> 00:05:21.640
- This is a move we saw Chucky make

00:05:21.640 --> 00:05:23.049
to scare Damian in the beginning of Bride

00:05:23.049 --> 00:05:24.570
which at the time I mentioned

00:05:24.570 --> 00:05:26.140
as being a reference to The Exorcist

00:05:26.140 --> 00:05:27.207
but I guess now he's just absorbed

00:05:27.207 --> 00:05:28.970
that into his own repertoire.

00:05:28.970 --> 00:05:30.550
We see it again later in the film.

00:05:30.550 --> 00:05:32.140
Nica would soon discover the truth

00:05:32.140 --> 00:05:33.100
about Charles Lee Ray

00:05:33.100 --> 00:05:34.560
on the internet and the articles contain

00:05:34.560 --> 00:05:37.366
some previously unknown information.

00:05:37.366 --> 00:05:40.283
(thunder rumbling)

00:05:42.040 --> 00:05:43.600
Charles Lee Ray's crimes would eventually

00:05:43.600 --> 00:05:44.670
be covered on the podcast,

00:05:44.670 --> 00:05:46.380
Hackenslash nearly a decade later.

00:05:46.380 --> 00:05:47.900
If the character in the
world of Chucky wanted

00:05:47.900 --> 00:05:48.960
to listen to this podcast,

00:05:48.960 --> 00:05:51.480
a good option for them
would be Amazon Music.

