00:06:50.720 --> 00:06:51.650
You may be wondering

00:06:51.650 --> 00:06:53.850
why this movie is called Curse of Chucky.

00:06:53.850 --> 00:06:55.320
It could be that this doll is cursed

00:06:55.320 --> 00:06:57.121
by the soul of Charles
Lee Ray using voodoo

00:06:57.121 --> 00:06:59.771
but that happens all the
way back in the first movie.

00:07:01.252 --> 00:07:03.778
- [Chucky] Just keep your
(upbeat tone) mouth shut.

00:07:03.778 --> 00:07:06.150
- Chucky, stop cursing!

00:07:06.150 --> 00:07:08.580
- Oh so that's why it's
called Curse of Chucky.

00:07:08.580 --> 00:07:09.990
This is also a callback to a line

00:07:09.990 --> 00:07:11.390
from Tyler in Child's Play 3

00:07:11.390 --> 00:07:14.098
who is similarly not a fan
of Chucky's foul mouth.

00:07:14.098 --> 00:07:16.030
(upbeat tone)

00:07:16.030 --> 00:07:17.960
- Charles, stop swearing.

00:07:17.960 --> 00:07:19.958
- After Alice recounts the
obscene things Chucky said

00:07:19.958 --> 00:07:21.040
to her mom,

00:07:21.040 --> 00:07:23.340
she also mentions this curious detail.

00:07:23.340 --> 00:07:25.140
- [Alice] He said there is no God.

00:07:25.140 --> 00:07:27.343
- And we hear Chucky himself
say this later in the movie.

00:07:27.343 --> 00:07:29.660
- There is no God.

00:07:29.660 --> 00:07:31.610
- Kind of a strange
thing to say for someone

00:07:31.610 --> 00:07:33.040
who literally is only alive

00:07:33.040 --> 00:07:35.630
because an ancient voodoo God
lent him some of his power.

00:07:35.630 --> 00:07:37.380
Has Chucky forgotten about that or what?

00:07:37.380 --> 00:07:38.280
I guess maybe what he meant

00:07:38.280 --> 00:07:40.090
to say was your God doesn't exist.

00:07:40.090 --> 00:07:41.430
The voodoo stuff is a smaller part

00:07:41.430 --> 00:07:42.286
of the story than ever before

00:07:42.286 --> 00:07:44.020
but when we flashback to '88,

00:07:44.020 --> 00:07:45.880
the room that Charles
holds Sarah Pierce captive

00:07:45.880 --> 00:07:47.690
in is decorated with voodoo artifacts

00:07:47.690 --> 00:07:48.770
and the knife that he uses

00:07:48.770 --> 00:07:51.180
to maim her pregnant belly
has a white snake on it.

00:07:51.180 --> 00:07:53.580
If you've seen my Horror
History episode on Damballa,

00:07:53.580 --> 00:07:56.240
the Haitian deity that Charles
calls upon to transfer souls,

00:07:56.240 --> 00:07:57.457
you know that in the Voodoo religion,

00:07:57.457 --> 00:07:59.870
Damballa is believed to
be a white snake being,

00:07:59.870 --> 00:08:01.930
which we see briefly
painted on Charles's wall

00:08:01.930 --> 00:08:02.930
in Child's Play 1.

00:08:02.930 --> 00:08:04.390
If you don't watch Horror History,

00:08:04.390 --> 00:08:05.380
you're a (upbeat tone) loser,

00:08:05.380 --> 00:08:06.340
go back to rolling around

00:08:06.340 --> 00:08:08.520
in a bathtub full of
Cheetos and eating them.

00:08:08.520 --> 00:08:10.150
Early on, Curse of Chucky focuses

00:08:10.150 --> 00:08:12.210
on building its own characters
and atmosphere rather

00:08:12.210 --> 00:08:14.250
than continuing the story
from the previous movies.

00:08:14.250 --> 00:08:15.900
When Nica contacts the delivery company

00:08:15.900 --> 00:08:17.270
to find out where the doll was sent from,

00:08:17.270 --> 00:08:19.110
she hears the words, evidence depository,

00:08:19.110 --> 00:08:21.310
meaning that something happened
between the end of Seed,

00:08:21.310 --> 00:08:23.014
where Chucky was in pieces around LA

00:08:23.014 --> 00:08:24.360
and the beginning of Curse,

00:08:24.360 --> 00:08:25.445
where he's put together and mailed.

00:08:25.445 --> 00:08:26.405
I think we're supposed to assume

00:08:26.405 --> 00:08:28.560
that the police eventually
collected the pieces

00:08:28.560 --> 00:08:30.640
and Tiffany acquired
them and reassembled him,

00:08:30.640 --> 00:08:31.700
just like she did in the opening

00:08:31.700 --> 00:08:33.317
of Bride where we see
Chucky's remains locked up

00:08:33.317 --> 00:08:35.100
in an evidence room.

00:08:35.100 --> 00:08:37.130
The movie doesn't really
acknowledge the older films

00:08:37.130 --> 00:08:39.390
at all until Nica
researches the doll's past.

00:08:39.390 --> 00:08:40.310
The search results rank

00:08:40.310 --> 00:08:42.020
from the most recent events to the oldest,

00:08:42.020 --> 00:08:44.440
starting with the unsolved
Los Angeles Homicide website

00:08:44.440 --> 00:08:45.840
that details the events of Seed,

00:08:45.840 --> 00:08:48.390
then the Niagara Falls and
Hackensack Homicide links,

00:08:48.390 --> 00:08:49.570
in both locations that Chucky

00:08:49.570 --> 00:08:50.950
and Tiffany terrorized in Bride,

00:08:50.950 --> 00:08:52.910
then there's the Kent
Military Academy Homicide

00:08:52.910 --> 00:08:55.260
investigation from the
aftermath of Child's Play 3,

00:08:55.260 --> 00:08:56.810
the Chicago Double Homicide case

00:08:56.810 --> 00:08:58.470
which involves Kevin and Joane Simpson

00:08:58.470 --> 00:09:01.620
from Child's Play 2 and finally
the Chicago Triple Homicide,

00:09:01.620 --> 00:09:02.890
AKA, Aunt Maggie,

00:09:02.890 --> 00:09:05.740
Eddie Caputo and Dr.
Ardmore in Child's Play 1.

00:09:05.740 --> 00:09:07.590
Nica then looks at newspaper archives

00:09:07.590 --> 00:09:09.730
which mention that Charles
Lee Ray was the chief suspect

00:09:09.730 --> 00:09:10.583
of a local kidnapping.

00:09:10.583 --> 00:09:13.570
This is an early reveal of what
we learn later in the movie,

00:09:13.570 --> 00:09:15.223
Sarah Pierce is the
woman who was kidnapped.

00:09:15.223 --> 00:09:17.910
Of course, this text isn't on
screen long enough to read it,

00:09:17.910 --> 00:09:19.093
but I love when there
are little clues like

00:09:19.093 --> 00:09:20.710
that that you can go back to.

00:09:20.710 --> 00:09:22.224
Her research is interrupted
when the electricity

00:09:22.224 --> 00:09:23.610
in the house goes haywire

00:09:23.610 --> 00:09:25.950
because upstairs, Chucky
kicked over a bucket of water

00:09:25.950 --> 00:09:27.500
to electrocute the nanny, Jill.

00:09:27.500 --> 00:09:29.910
This is seriously the worst
outlet placement ever.

00:09:29.910 --> 00:09:31.606
Was this house designed by EA?

00:09:31.606 --> 00:09:36.606
- Women, can't live with them, period.

00:09:36.612 --> 00:09:38.840
(Chucky giggling)

00:09:38.840 --> 00:09:40.730
That might be a reference
to Bride of Chucky,

00:09:40.730 --> 00:09:42.224
where Chuck and his woman
literally just bicker

00:09:42.224 --> 00:09:43.690
for the entire movie.

00:09:43.690 --> 00:09:45.460
Also, you have to wonder what was going

00:09:45.460 --> 00:09:47.404
through Barb's head during this scene.

00:09:47.404 --> 00:09:50.071
(ominous music)

00:09:55.540 --> 00:09:57.066
I don't know what Tiffany was
complaining about in Bride,

00:09:57.066 --> 00:09:58.830
okay, it's a knife.

00:09:58.830 --> 00:09:59.754
But this scene showcases one

00:09:59.754 --> 00:10:01.540
of the cool things about this movie

00:10:01.540 --> 00:10:02.704
which is that Chucky has gotten better

00:10:02.704 --> 00:10:04.140
at being a killer doll.

00:10:04.140 --> 00:10:05.032
Gone are the days of him trying

00:10:05.032 --> 00:10:07.610
to overpower people who are
four times bigger than him.

00:10:07.610 --> 00:10:10.450
Now, it's all about surprise
and psychological manipulation,

00:10:10.450 --> 00:10:12.152
which is honestly way
scarier and the choice

00:10:12.152 --> 00:10:14.240
to have Nica in a wheelchair is brilliant

00:10:14.240 --> 00:10:16.590
because when there finally
is a physical confrontation,

00:10:16.590 --> 00:10:18.640
her handicap really
levels the playing field.

00:10:18.640 --> 00:10:19.473
In my previous episodes,

00:10:19.473 --> 00:10:21.546
I talked about how the Bride
in Seed arc was influenced

00:10:21.546 --> 00:10:22.950
by the Scream franchise

00:10:22.950 --> 00:10:25.084
but between the focus on
suspense rather than violence,

00:10:25.084 --> 00:10:26.770
the twist ending and the use

00:10:26.770 --> 00:10:28.290
of a disabled character who finds a way

00:10:28.290 --> 00:10:29.890
to use her disability to her advantage,

00:10:29.890 --> 00:10:31.770
I'm guessing Curse
might have been inspired

00:10:31.770 --> 00:10:33.400
by the works of M Night Shyamalan.

00:10:33.400 --> 00:10:35.152
Seriously, Nica using her own legs

00:10:35.152 --> 00:10:38.290
as an axe board is the biggest
alpha move I've ever seen.

00:10:38.290 --> 00:10:41.020
I don't know why Ian doesn't
try to stop the axe whatsoever,

00:10:41.020 --> 00:10:42.920
but whatever, Nica's the last one now.

00:10:42.920 --> 00:10:44.860
She uses that axe to
cut Chucky's head off,

00:10:44.860 --> 00:10:45.693
something that happens

00:10:45.693 --> 00:10:48.060
to him in both Child's
Play 1 and Seed of Chucky

00:10:48.060 --> 00:10:49.630
but this time is notably different

00:10:49.630 --> 00:10:51.030
because his head just pops off

00:10:51.030 --> 00:10:52.460
like you'd expect a doll head to.

00:10:52.460 --> 00:10:53.550
There's no blood or guts,

00:10:53.550 --> 00:10:55.330
which means he probably
hasn't been resurrected

00:10:55.330 --> 00:10:57.620
for very long and hasn't
started to turn human yet,

00:10:57.620 --> 00:10:58.990
as he does in the other movies.

00:10:58.990 --> 00:11:00.820
Although the consistency
with this rule is about

00:11:00.820 --> 00:11:03.040
as consistent as my
Instagram posting schedule.

00:11:03.040 --> 00:11:04.650
As usual, Chucky getting dismembered

00:11:04.650 --> 00:11:06.250
does not slow him down and he launches

00:11:06.250 --> 00:11:07.960
into a flashback of everything that led up

00:11:07.960 --> 00:11:10.260
to his original death in
the opening of Child's Play.

00:11:10.260 --> 00:11:11.140
In his flashback,

00:11:11.140 --> 00:11:12.186
you can actually see the home video

00:11:12.186 --> 00:11:14.271
that the Pierce family
watch earlier being filmed,

00:11:14.271 --> 00:11:16.300
I thought that was a kind of cool detail.

00:11:16.300 --> 00:11:18.470
The flashback also ties
together some loose threads

00:11:18.470 --> 00:11:19.620
from the beginning of the movie.

00:11:19.620 --> 00:11:21.880
Remember how I pointed out the
mother's medication bottles,

00:11:21.880 --> 00:11:23.380
letting us know that she isn't well?

00:11:23.380 --> 00:11:24.380
In the home movie scene,

00:11:24.380 --> 00:11:25.620
Barb mentions that this started

00:11:25.620 --> 00:11:27.540
around the time that
their dad passed away.

00:11:27.540 --> 00:11:29.150
- A couple weeks before Nica was born,

00:11:29.150 --> 00:11:30.600
Mom was never the same after that.

00:11:30.600 --> 00:11:31.660
- We're led to believe one

00:11:31.660 --> 00:11:33.840
or both of these events
affected Sarah's mental health

00:11:33.840 --> 00:11:34.673
but the flashback shows us

00:11:34.673 --> 00:11:37.700
it was actually her being
kidnapped by Charles Lee Ray.

00:11:37.700 --> 00:11:38.760
He brings her sunflowers

00:11:38.760 --> 00:11:39.902
while she's in captivity and this explains

00:11:39.902 --> 00:11:41.770
why she's seen painting a sunflower

00:11:41.770 --> 00:11:43.580
in the opening and why her attic is filled

00:11:43.580 --> 00:11:44.850
with artwork of these sunflowers,

00:11:44.850 --> 00:11:46.274
it's basically some
kind of coping mechanism

00:11:46.274 --> 00:11:48.770
for the horrors that
Charles subjected her to.

00:11:48.770 --> 00:11:51.530
Nica is just the next target
in Sarah's family tree

00:11:51.530 --> 00:11:53.120
but when the police arrive, Chucky goes

00:11:53.120 --> 00:11:54.714
into Barbie mode and she
ends up getting blamed

00:11:54.714 --> 00:11:56.090
for all the murders.

00:11:56.090 --> 00:11:57.840
They could have ended
the movie right there

00:11:57.840 --> 00:11:58.673
and I would have been satisfied

00:11:58.673 --> 00:12:00.934
but what we get instead is
an additional six minutes

00:12:00.934 --> 00:12:02.710
of fan-service for enthusiasts

00:12:02.710 --> 00:12:04.194
of the Chucky continuity and honestly,

00:12:04.194 --> 00:12:06.520
I'm here for it and it's totally packed

00:12:06.520 --> 00:12:07.570
with interesting details,

00:12:07.570 --> 00:12:09.096
including the previously unknown fate

00:12:09.096 --> 00:12:11.325
of beloved legacy characters.

00:12:11.325 --> 00:12:14.242
(thunder rumbling)

00:12:17.470 --> 00:12:20.550
(spooky dance music)

00:12:20.550 --> 00:12:21.383
After the trial,

00:12:21.383 --> 00:12:23.270
this police officer takes
the Chucky doll along

00:12:23.270 --> 00:12:24.103
in his squad car

00:12:24.103 --> 00:12:25.493
and what would follow is
almost an exact recreation

00:12:25.493 --> 00:12:27.470
of the opening of Bride of Chucky,

00:12:27.470 --> 00:12:29.205
where he makes a phone
call where he mentions,

00:12:29.205 --> 00:12:30.780
- Don't forget my money.
- Don't forget my money.

00:12:30.780 --> 00:12:31.888
- [Zac] And investigates
the evidence bag right

00:12:31.888 --> 00:12:33.710
before getting his throat slit from

00:12:33.710 --> 00:12:35.210
behind by Tiffany's nail file,

00:12:35.210 --> 00:12:37.230
yes, she uses the same one from Bride.

00:12:37.230 --> 00:12:39.440
Then we see her shipping
Chucky to a new destination

00:12:39.440 --> 00:12:41.890
which makes a lot more sense
than Chucky shipping himself

00:12:41.890 --> 00:12:43.350
in three and five and he arrives

00:12:43.350 --> 00:12:45.820
at Alice's new home and tells
her that he wants to play.

00:12:45.820 --> 00:12:50.600
- [Chucky] And now it's time to play.

00:12:50.600 --> 00:12:51.731
- Hide and Seek?

00:12:51.731 --> 00:12:53.580
- Hide the Soul.

00:12:53.580 --> 00:12:55.240
- Hide The Soul is the
same name of the game

00:12:55.240 --> 00:12:56.090
that he uses when he was trying

00:12:56.090 --> 00:12:58.808
to perform the Damballa chant
on Tyler in the third movie.

00:12:58.808 --> 00:13:00.646
- [Tyler] Couldn't we
just play hide and seek,

00:13:00.646 --> 00:13:02.979
what do you call this game anyway?

00:13:02.979 --> 00:13:05.020
- Hide the Soul.

00:13:05.020 --> 00:13:06.448
- We are led to believe
that he's successful,

00:13:06.448 --> 00:13:08.169
making this his first successful transfer

00:13:08.169 --> 00:13:10.370
from the doll body into a human body.

00:13:10.370 --> 00:13:11.849
Again, they could have
ended the movie there,

00:13:11.849 --> 00:13:13.680
and I probably would have been satisfied

00:13:13.680 --> 00:13:15.810
but we would have missed out
on the post credits scene.

00:13:15.810 --> 00:13:17.620
For the first time in over 14 years,

00:13:17.620 --> 00:13:19.170
we're reintroduced to Andy Barclay,

00:13:19.170 --> 00:13:20.960
who receives a package before his birthday

00:13:20.960 --> 00:13:23.240
from the hottest delivery
person that I've ever seen.

00:13:23.240 --> 00:13:26.080
We hear him on the phone with
his mom when he says this.

00:13:26.080 --> 00:13:27.960
- Yeah, I'm definitely coming
for my birthday tomorrow.

00:13:27.960 --> 00:13:29.210
- Back in the original movie,

00:13:29.210 --> 00:13:31.610
Chucky was his birthday
present from his mom to him,

00:13:31.610 --> 00:13:33.810
which means Chucky is
attacking him one day shy

00:13:33.810 --> 00:13:35.620
of the anniversary of their first meeting.

00:13:35.620 --> 00:13:36.453
He also asks.

00:13:36.453 --> 00:13:37.920
- [Andy] How's mike doing?

00:13:37.920 --> 00:13:39.750
He's presumably talking about Mike Norris,

00:13:39.750 --> 00:13:41.167
the police officer that helped save him

00:13:41.167 --> 00:13:42.870
and his mom all of those years ago.

00:13:42.870 --> 00:13:44.215
It's nice to see that they kept in touch.

00:13:44.215 --> 00:13:46.890
There are a lot of interesting
items in Andy's apartment.

00:13:46.890 --> 00:13:49.140
We see a picture of him and
his mom from when he was six,

00:13:49.140 --> 00:13:51.010
a picture of Kyle from Child's Play 2

00:13:51.010 --> 00:13:53.210
which is actually a clue that
they're still in contact,

00:13:53.210 --> 00:13:54.730
as we would see in the next movie.

00:13:54.730 --> 00:13:55.645
You can also see his diploma

00:13:55.645 --> 00:13:57.310
from Kent Military Academy,

00:13:57.310 --> 00:13:58.990
which tells us that
despite getting arrested

00:13:58.990 --> 00:14:00.130
at the end of Child's Play 3,

00:14:00.130 --> 00:14:02.270
he was still able to
finish school and graduate,

00:14:02.270 --> 00:14:04.060
which also kind of leads
into the next movie,

00:14:04.060 --> 00:14:05.900
Cult of Chucky, where
we see his familiarity

00:14:05.900 --> 00:14:08.420
with guns from the academy has
stuck with him over the years

00:14:08.420 --> 00:14:10.330
but if you wanna hear me
talk about Cult of Chucky,

00:14:10.330 --> 00:14:11.908
then you'll have to join
me in the next episode

00:14:11.908 --> 00:14:13.290
of Things You Missed.

00:14:13.290 --> 00:14:14.123
When that video comes out,

00:14:14.123 --> 00:14:15.560
you'll find it there on the left,

00:14:15.560 --> 00:14:16.977
but in the meantime,
make sure you subscribe

00:14:16.977 --> 00:14:19.420
to CZsWorld for new horrors every week,

00:14:19.420 --> 00:14:21.399
ring the death bell and
select all notifications

00:14:21.399 --> 00:14:23.870
and I will see you in the next one,

00:14:23.870 --> 00:14:26.049
assuming we both survive.

00:14:26.049 --> 00:14:28.632
(upbeat music)

